('127.769.d.19.D',4,'Blow fly larvae are useful in estimating time of death because:','["they appear at random", "they develop in predictable stages", "they never reach a body", "they live indefinitely"]'::jsonb,1,'Predictable growth.','original'),
('127.769.d.20.A',3,'A student labels the skull, femur, humerus and pelvis on a model of the human skeleton. This identifies:','["muscles of the heart", "organs of the gut", "the major bones of the human skeletal system", "nerves of the skin"]'::jsonb,2,'Skeleton bones.','original'),
('127.769.d.20.A',4,'The longest bone in the human body is the:','["tibia", "humerus", "radius", "femur"]'::jsonb,3,'Femur is longest.','original'),
('127.769.d.20.B',3,'A forensic anthropologist examines a bone fragment under a microscope and sees a pattern of structure unlike that of a deer. This compares the composition and structure of:','["human and non-human bones", "wood and metal", "paper and cloth", "glass and plastic"]'::jsonb,0,'Bone microstructure differs.','original'),
('127.769.d.20.B',4,'One way to tell whether a bone is human is to look at its:','["smell", "microscopic structure and shape", "price", "color only"]'::jsonb,1,'Histology and shape.','original'),
('127.769.d.20.C',3,'At a field recovery, workers photograph bones in place, record locations and wrap them in paper to protect them. This describes the collection and preservation of:','["ink evidence", "fiber evidence", "bone evidence", "glass evidence"]'::jsonb,2,'Document before removing.','original'),
('127.769.d.20.D',3,'An anthropologist studies the pelvis, the skull and the length of the long bones to estimate a person''s sex, age and height. This explains the characteristics indicative of:','["a person''s music taste", "a person''s favorite food", "a person''s address", "a person''s biological profile"]'::jsonb,3,'Biological profile.','original'),
('127.769.d.20.D',4,'The pelvis is useful for estimating sex because it:','["differs in shape between males and females", "is made of cartilage", "is always identical", "changes color"]'::jsonb,0,'Pelvic shape differences.','original'),
('127.769.d.20.C',4,'Bone evidence should be stored in a:','["wet plastic bag", "dry paper container to prevent mold", "sealed jar of water", "open box in sunlight"]'::jsonb,1,'Dry paper avoids mold.','original'),
('127.769.d.20.E',3,'An odontologist compares X-rays taken before death with the teeth of an unidentified body to confirm who it is. This explains how remains are identified through:','["library records", "school records", "dental records", "phone records"]'::jsonb,2,'Dental records are unique.','original'),
('127.769.d.20.E',4,'Teeth are valuable for identification because they:','["rot quickly", "cannot be recorded", "look the same in all people", "resist decay and have unique features"]'::jsonb,3,'Durable and unique.','original')
